## Arguments Reference

All arguments are optional; settings that are not configured keep their current value.

* `enabled` - (Optional) Whether the MFA method is enabled.
* `host` - (Optional) Host name of the Okta organization, e.g. `example.okta.com`.
* `access_key` - (Optional) Okta API token. The value is sensitive. When the API does not return the value, the known value is kept in state, and it must be configured, because the update would clear it.
* `identity_attribute` - (Optional) Identity attribute that maps identities to Okta users, e.g. `email`.

## Attributes Reference

In addition to the arguments, the following attributes are exported; arguments that are not configured show the current tenant value.

* `id` - Always `mfa-okta-config`.
* `mfa_method` - MFA method name (`okta-verify`).

